confirmed.detail:
Warm.run returns immediately when `_envs.has(tag)`, and main.gd:955 passes the same tag "ex" for both desert and lab.

The ex tier builds the mob list from `host.level.map_id` (_ex_mob_list) and runs the 8-direction scene sweep. So only the first new map entered in a session is warmed. When the second map is entered, none of the following are prewarmed:
- its mobs, elites and bosses (lab: zombie / mech_* / gel_mutant RGBA, plus the doctor model);
- the lab's additive 禁制光幕 curtain material (a different variant from the desert's fogged one);
- the scene sweep around the new spawn.

P_fix only documented the hero-switch case (剑门 not prewarmed). This is wider: any lab-only material compiles mid-raid on the web/compatibility renderer, where P_fix measured about 1 s per new shader and multi-second frames for the gate.

